{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2YbjLaPUYBjgunnLVT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause was mutable default arguments in `inv/warehouse.py`. `Warehouse.__init__` had `stock={}` and `history=[]`, and `restock` had `tags=[]`. Python evaluates those defaults once, at function definition, so every `Warehouse` created without explicit arguments shared the same dict and list. That is why a second warehouse saw the first one's stock and why `restock` on one changed the other.\n\n**Fix** (`inv/warehouse.py`):\n- `__init__` now takes `stock=None` and `history=None` and creates a fresh `{}` / `[]` per instance when they are `None`.\n- `restock` now takes `tags=None`. A new `Item` gets its own copy (`list(tags)`) or a fresh empty list. Before, every item created with the default shared one `tags` list, which was the same bug in a different spot.\n\nThe test is unchanged. I did not work around it in the test.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `tests/test_inv.py::test_independent_warehouses` failed before the change (`assert {'bolt': 5} == {}`) and passes now. `pytest tests/` reports 1 passed.\n- A manual check confirmed two warehouses with the same SKU keep separate stock (`{'bolt': 5}` vs `{'bolt': 2}`), separate histories, and separate `tags` lists.\n\n**Regressions:** The only callers in the repo are the test file, so the public API is unchanged. The `stock` and `history` parameters still work when passed explicitly, and passing an explicit dict or list still uses that object. `hooks/subagent_stop.py` is unrelated to the inventory code.\n\nNothing is committed. The changes are in the working tree for you to review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4582,"cache_read_input_tokens":30223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4582},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37cb3c5e-8284-4002-b173-afd6816c6237","uuid":"7be0db07-2436-4238-bf78-52388472d9af","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:05:26.302Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs2YbSz62x4qxGdsprL8"}
